From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:49:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/25] sglang DSA: record the post-convergence validation

Re-ran the full validation on the converged branch, because dropping the nextn
diff moved that fix onto a different code path (main's idempotent patch script,
run earlier in the same Dockerfile) and "the two make the identical edit" was a
static argument, not a measurement.

From an image built by Dockerfile.sglang on both nodes, no in-container patching:
4/4 probe with acc_len 2.00-3.43, 32/32, 128/128 twice, 0 Traceback /
KVTransferError in either leg, all 8 DP ranks serving, 0 retries.

Confirmed the nextn edit is main's and not ours: the line in the running image
carries no trailing comment, and the build log shows [glm52-nextn] patched
followed by our PREREQ assert reading src=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
